# One person, four spellings. `cgai00247@gmail.com` is a typo of
# `cgai00742@gmail.com` -- transposed digits -- and it is the address git was
# configured with, so it carries the majority of the history. The config is
# fixed; this file makes the record already written read correctly, without
# rewriting any commit.
#
# Left of the angle brackets is the canonical identity. Everything after it is
# an alias that maps onto it.
CG <cgai00742@gmail.com> <cgai00247@gmail.com>
CG <cgai00742@gmail.com> Christopher Guerrero <cgai00742@gmail.com>

# Claude-assisted commits keep their own attribution. Anthropic's terms assign
# rights in the output to the user, so this is a record of how the work was
# done, not a second rights-holder.
